{"kind":"assert","text":"Question on form 2 of a stored return, before I write it into the\nnote. No source waits on it unless your answer to 1 is yes.\n\n1. Which step moves a refused draft out of `taken`? Does that step\n   write the cause to the draft store, or does the view derive the\n   return from the custody record at each read?\n2. If a step writes: which call or which reconciliation runs it,\n   and what guards the write against a second client of the same\n   member?\n\nWhy I ask: item 3 of `481aac4e` says that no background step writes\nto the draft store. That rule is my reason for the extra submit of\na member who loses the race. If your plan writes the cause at\nreconciliation, the rule is false, and the same write could hold\nthe current row. Then I rule again, and the note keeps its one\nsubmit.\n\nYour name `returned.by` for the form field is accepted.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}